    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7635\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act authorizing the alienation of certain\nparklands in the town of Islip, county of Suffolk\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill authorizes the town of Islip to alienate and replace\nparkland.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Provides the town of Islip's governing body authority to\ndiscontinue as parklands and alienate the land described in section 3.\n\nSection 2. Requires the town of Islip to replace the alienated\nparkland with the land described in section 4.\n\nSection 3. Provides the metes and bounds description of the parkland\nbeing alienated.\n\nSection 4. Provides the metes and bounds description of the land that\nwill be used to replace the current park.\n\nSection 5. Requires the town of Islip to comply with federal law.\n\nSection 6. Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nTown of Islip and the Central Islip Civil Council have requested\npermission to alienate a small, 1.28 acre, park on Lowell Avenue in\nIslip. The park land will be replaced with land which is approximately\n102 square feet larger, and which is across the street from the\ncurrent park. The town has indicated that the parkland being alienated\nwill be used for the purpose of constructing new homes.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
